  "question": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/a528e366-fdce-4841-b6ea-3e4d9f760505.png\" style=\"width: 400px; height: 150px;\" /></p><p>The figure shows a liquid of given density flowing steadily in horizontal tube of varying cross-section. Cross-sectional areas at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>cm</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>25</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mm</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo></math> if the speed of liquid at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>60</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>&#8211;</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></math> is</p><p>(Given&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></math>&nbsp;are liquid pressures at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> points.</p><p>Density&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#961;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1000</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;are on the axis of tube)</p>",
